{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"151ae5e4e8fbb9606e9b1c6962426b2ac8ecd1fa6fd08377743a6152b8d160df","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar-gerrit-voter-errors alarm (CloudWatch monitoring)","key_entities":["aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.voter_errors","infra/terraform/monitoring_s4b.tf","rebar/host:voter_errors","evaluation_periods","datapoints_to_alarm","RECONCILE_INTERVAL_SECONDS","observability.sh","terraform-drift.yml","infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md"],"problem_keywords":["alarm noise","transient errors","sustained failure detection","voter errors","false positives"],"propositions":["The rebar-gerrit-voter-errors alarm fires on single transient self-healing errors within a 5-minute window, producing false-positive pages that do not require operator action.","Sustained voter failures (expired token, LLM outage, Gerrit down) emit continuous marker streams across consecutive evaluation periods and must trigger alerts reliably.","The alarm shape must discriminate persistence (markers across multiple periods) rather than magnitude to suppress isolated transient spikes while catching genuine stuck gates.","Recalibrate the alarm from 1-of-1 (Sum>0 over 300s) to 3-of-5 (datapoints_to_alarm=3, evaluation_periods=5) to fire on sustained failures within ~15 minutes while remaining immune to boundary-straddling single transients."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787725142587815001,"uuid":"00f2daf8-f73c-447e-9a84-895f047981ab"}